{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "note-main",
      "type": "canvas_note",
      "position": { "x": -10, "y": -165 },
      "style": { "width": 1390, "height": 135 },
      "width": 1390,
      "height": 135,
      "data": {
        "label": "Note",
        "params": {
          "color_index": 3,
          "text": "**RANSAC Homography** — Robust geometric alignment between two views of the same scene.\n\n1. **SIFT** extracts scale-invariant keypoints + descriptors in both images.\n2. **Brute-Force matching** (Lowe ratio test) removes ambiguous candidate matches.\n3. **RANSAC** iteratively estimates H, rejects outliers — only geometrically consistent matches survive.\n4. Outputs: warped image (img1 aligned to img2's frame), inlier match overlay, and the 3×3 homography matrix.\n\n**Setup — synthetic demo:** The Python node rotates the source portrait 20° to produce img2. RANSAC should recover a near-perfect rotation. Replace both sources with two photos of the same real scene (different angle, sensor, or scale) to see outlier filtering in action."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-tip",
      "type": "canvas_note",
      "position": { "x": 606, "y": 75 },
      "style": { "width": 308, "height": 115 },
      "width": 308,
      "height": 115,
      "data": {
        "label": "Note",
        "params": {
          "color_index": 5,
          "text": "**RANSAC parameters**\n- **Lowe ratio** (0.6–0.8): lower = stricter match filter\n- **RANSAC threshold**: max reprojection error in pixels (try 3–8)\n- **Min inliers**: reject H if too few points survive\n- **Model**: Homography for planar/far scenes; Affine for rigid 3D + small baseline"
        }
      }
    },
